  }
 },
 "requested_at": "2026-11-13T20:10:09.845757Z",
 "text": "In Ontario, a landlord is strictly prohibited from collecting a damage deposit. Under section 105 of the *Residential Tenancies Act, 2006*, the only security deposit a landlord may lawfully collect is a rent deposit (commonly known as last month's rent) collected in accordance with section 106. Because a $500 deposit held to ensure the unit is left in good condition is a security deposit other than a lawful rent deposit, it violates section 105 (and is consequently void under section 4 of the Act).\n\nVerdict: not enforceable\nSection: 105",
